o the 5×5 frames. In that case no frame was ever compared or filled. The copying rule itself still matches every diff in the fact sheet:\n\n- Each empty frame receives the 3×3 interior of the patterned frame of the same colour.\n- Pair 1: the colour-2 \"T\" goes into both empty colour-2 frames, and the 6 and 8 patterns go into their partners.\n- Pair 2: the colour-2 pattern and the single 8 dot are copied.\n- Pair 3: the 3 dot and the 2, 8 and 1 patterns are copied.\n- Pair 4: the colour-4 pattern is copied.\n\nI will now find the frames directly as objects instead of through the dividers. Each frame is a same-colour connected component whose bounding box is at least 3×3. Any part of the pattern that touches the frame belongs to that component. A pattern part that does not touch the frame, such as an isolated centre dot, is its own small object, and the size filter removes it. For each frame:\n\n1. Use the frame's bounding box.\n2. Read the interior: everything strictly inside the box.\n3. Group the frames by colour.\n4. For each colour, take the interior of the frame that is not blank.\n5. Stamp that interior into every blank frame of the same colour.\n\nOn the test input, this copies:\n- the colour-8 corner shape into the two empty 8 frames,\n- the colour-3 diagonal into the empty 3 frame,\n- the colour-6 shape into the empty 6 frame,\n- the colour-2 pattern into the three empty 2 frames.\n\nColour 7 has only one frame, so there is nowhere to copy its pattern. Colour 1 has no patterned frame, so its frames stay empty.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    bg = background(g)\n    frames = {}\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        if y1 - y0 < 2 or x1 - x0 < 2:\n            continue\n        frames.setdefault(o[\"colour\"], []).append((y0, x0, y1, x1))\n    for c in sorted(frames):\n        bl = frames[c]\n        pattern = None\n        for (y0, x0, y1, x1) in bl:\n            inner = g[y0+1:y1, x0+1:x1]\n            if (inner != bg).any():\n                pattern = inner.copy()\n                break\n        if pattern is None:\n            continue\n        changed = False\n        for (y0, x0, y1, x1) in bl:\n            inner = g[y0+1:y1, x0+1:x1]\n            if not (inner != bg).any() and inner.shape == pattern.shape:\n                g[y0+1:y1, x0+1:x1] = pattern\n                changed = True\n        if changed:\n            emit(g, f\"Copy the interior pattern of the patterned colour-{c} frame into every empty colour-{c} frame.\")\n    emit(g, \"Every empty frame with a patterned same-colour partner now carries that pattern.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"objects":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each frame is a same-colour connected component whose bounding box is at least 3×3."}],"panels":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The likely cause is `panels()`."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"It relies on the dividers, and the dividers here are background-coloured lines, so it probably did not split the grid into the 5×5 frames."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"I will now find the frames directly as objects instead of through the dividers."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Stamp that interior into every blank frame of the same colour."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Each empty frame receives the 3×3 interior of the patterned frame of the same colour."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Read the interior: everything strictly inside the box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"For each colour, take the interior of the frame that is not blank."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each frame is a same-colour connected component whose bounding box is at least 3×3."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Use the frame's bounding box."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"bfbea8c9fc706a305e3